course: dictionary
lesson: 8234
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around the word and ask: what meaning would fit here? «The Industrial Revolution began in Britain around 1760, when people began making things with machines in factories.» Here revolution means a very big change in how people live and work.
explain: «The wheel makes 60 revolutions a minute.» This is not about a change in government. Revolutions here are full turns around a centre. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The wheel makes 60 full turns a minute" still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
explain: The same word can work in different subjects. In maths, one revolution is a full turn of 360°, so half a revolution is 180°. In science, the Earth makes one revolution around the Sun each year. Each time, the clues in the sentence tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Revolution has more than one meaning, so always check the context.
fact: A revolution can be a very big change, such as the Industrial Revolution.
fact: A revolution can also be one complete turn around a centre: one full revolution is 360°.
fact: The Earth takes one year to make one revolution around the Sun.
fact: Speeds of turning are given as «revolutions per minute», shortened to rpm.
exercise: What does revolution mean in «The Industrial Revolution began in Britain around 1760»? | The Earth's journey around the Sun | A short, rude reply | *A very big change in how people live and work | A full turn around a centre
exercise: «The wheel makes 60 revolutions a minute.» What does revolutions mean here? | Changes of government | Rude remarks made in a minute | Years of the Sun | *Full turns around a centre
exercise: How many degrees are in one full revolution? | 180 | *360 | 90 | 720
test: When people overthrow a government or ruler, often by force, what is that called? | *A revolution | A quiet meeting | A holiday | A rotation
test: Which sentence uses revolution to mean one complete turn? | The lesson began at nine | *The fan made ten revolutions in one second | The town had a new market | The French Revolution began in 1789
exam: In «Earth makes one revolution around the Sun each year», what does revolution mean? | A sudden change of government | A slow walk | *The Earth's journey around the Sun, which takes one year | A loud noise
